TUnit uses `[Before(...)]` / `[After(...)]` attributes with a scope parameter. Here's each level:

## 1. Before/After every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs before each [Test] in this class
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each [Test]
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsValid() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once per class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class CustomerApiTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client = new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://localhost") };
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task GetCustomer_Returns200() { /* use _client */ }
}
```

## 3. Once per assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start in-process WireMock server
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // tear down server
    }
}
```

## 4. Once per entire test session

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

## Summary table

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be | Context type |
|-------|-----------|---------------|--------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | instance | `TestContext` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | **static** | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | **static** | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | **static** | `TestSessionContext` |

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (static, in any class) for a *global* hook that fires for every test across the entire run—handy for logging or timing without modifying each test class.
